      },
      "message": "feat(post): a PathPilot (LinuxCNC) lathe post\n\nassets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps, registered as \"Tormach PathPilot Lathe\"\n(BUILTINS + LATHE_POSTS; the lathe default stays Fanuc Lathe). Specced\nfrom the LinuxCNC G-code reference and lathe page and Tormach's public\nPathPilot lathe programming pages: G7 diameter X, G18, G20/G21 from the\nmachine, G95 per-rev feeds, G97 / G96 D<max> S, G30 then T0101 (no M6),\nG2/G3 with radius I, threading as one merged G33 Z K per pass or - with\nthe Threading option - the one-block LinuxCNC G76 P Z I J R1 K Q0 H,\ndrilling on centre as plain moves with a G4 dwell in seconds. Refused by\nname: tapping, back-bore, off-axis holes, G76 records it cannot state\nexactly (compound infeed, finish allowance, pull-out, unequal rungs,\ninternal / -X threads), tool numbers outside T01-T99, nose-radius comp.\nThe UI threading picker shows for both lathe posts.\n\nGoldens: nc/tormach-lathe/{turning,thread_g33,thread_g76,axial_drill}\n_{mm,inch}.nc, pinned by lathe_post_tormach.rs with a LinuxCNC syntax\ncheck over every program; conformance lists the new post.\n\nRefs #612\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
