  {
    "sha": "24945aeced06f01e3802d29330df490ecf7a03ef",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDI0OTQ1YWVjZWQwNmYwMWUzODAyZDI5MzMwZGY0OTBlY2Y3YTAzZWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:21:28Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:21:28Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): the PathPilot lathe post takes the stated thread hand and the tool's control point\n\nAdapts tormach-lathe.cps to the merged lathe stream (#629, #630, #641,\n#632) and fixes the two post defects the Hub kit build recorded.\n\n- threadHands = true: M3, or M4 (with a mount-for-M4 note) under PARAM\n  SpindleDirection reverse; each G33 half-turn's arc sense is checked\n  against the section's spindle and a mismatch refused by name; a G76\n  record whose hand and Z direction disagree with the spindle refused.\n  G33/G76 cut from the top toward EndZ (the chuck), as the stream does.\n- The stream point is the tool's control point: the tool note states\n  ORIENTATION n; goldens shift X-1.6 Z-0.8 for the r0.8 orientation-2\n  insert (finish now on the Ø7 neck and the Z2 shoulder).\n- G33 K is one number per thread (the THREAD record's lead), half-turns\n  merge within a 2.5 um lattice allowance - a 12 TPI lead no longer\n  splits a pass into blocks with different K.\n- G76 words on the control's grid: I J K computed once in grid steps,\n  root rounded outward (never deeper than the minor), J shallower; the\n  diameter/height checks allow the stream lattice (2.5 um) so a legal\n  cycle is not refused. Word order P Z I J K R Q H (PathPilot's\n  conversational order); R1/Q0/H from the record; no D (undocumented in\n  LinuxCNC's and Tormach's G76).\n- Suites split: lathe_post_tormach (turning/drill/dialect) and\n  lathe_post_tormach_thread (G33/G76/hand), fixtures in\n  tests/tormach_lathe_support.\n\nRefs #612\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
