      },
      "message": "fix(post): lathe posts reset surface speed at each section's end\n\nA section's SurfaceSpeed PARAM set sCss and nothing reset it, so a\nlater section that stated none still posted G96 with the machine-max\ncap instead of its own G97 S<rpm> - a drill on centre would run at the\nspindle maximum. Both lathe posts (Fanuc, PathPilot) now clear sCss in\nendPreamble(), beside the other per-section asks. Pinned by a\ntwo-section stream (CSS turning, then an axial drill with no CSS) in\neach post's suite.\n\nFixes #772\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
